  "status_text": "Out of more than a trillion trillion possible keys, does even one pass both tests? At 10:20 the checker accepted a proof that one circuit answers for every pair of 100-bit names when each test runs for three rounds. Its budget is 50,000 times 2^50 AND/OR/NOT gates, each reading at most two earlier wires. That is less than one gate per 20 billion possible keys. The checked bound covers every key width from 20 bits on (L-meta-25483). The bench is tracking what extra rounds cost.",
